    "G_G1": "Plan C Logistic CDI model achieved calibration slope 1.1353 (within [0.85, 1.15]) and Brier 0.1353 (< 0.175), beating base rate 0.2490. However, its 10-bin Expected Calibration Error (ECE) is 0.0905, exceeding the strict pre-registered gate threshold of 0.0400. In middle bins [0.3, 0.7), 2026 empirical win rates exceeded predicted probabilities due to heightened chasing success (56.7%) in modern IPL night matches.",
    "G_A2": "At Ball 0 (prior to first ball bowled), WP1 predicts historical environment baseline prior (~0.483). In the 2026 test set (N=136), batting-first win rate was 43.38%, yielding in-sample sample-mean variance Brier of 0.24562. The anonymous pre-match model achieved Brier 0.24586, failing to strictly beat the empirical test-set base rate by 0.00024. Deliveries from Ball 30 onward decisively beat baseline.",
    "G_A3": "Uncalibrated defense curve W(T) from DP lookup produced a test calibration slope of 0.3979 (pre-2026 training slope 0.5849). Platt scaling fitted strictly on pre-2026 matches (alpha=-0.1418, beta=0.5849) improved test slope to 0.6805 and test Brier to 0.1928, but remained below the pre-registered [0.80, 1.20] threshold due to structural DP variance compression relative to empirical match volatility."
